Load data from TAB delimited file:

1. Execute either
   FLUSH TABLES
   or
   mysqladmin flush-tables
   mysql -u gbrey -e 'FLUSH TABLES' ncsetoks_ewjload

2. Use 
   myisamchk --keys-used=0 -rq /path/to/db/tbl_name
   This removes all use of indexes for the table.

3. Insert data into the table with
   mysql -u gbrey -e 'LOAD DATA INFILE "/path/to/file.tab" INTO TABLE tokens' ncsetoks_ewj
   This does not update any indexes and therefore is very fast.

4. Re-create the indexes with
   myisamchk -rq /path/to/db/tbl_name
   This creates the index tree in memory before writing it to disk,
   which is much faster that updating the index during LOAD DATA INFILE
   because it avoids lots of disk seeks.
   The resulting index tree is also perfectly balanced.

5. Execute either
   FLUSH TABLES
   or
   mysqladmin flush-tables
   mysql -u gbrey -e 'FLUSH TABLES' ncsetoks_ewjload


